fb: drain the GPU to now before the panel reads a frame (0281)

The 0229 gate fences the GPU work submitted before the swap arrived. A
compositor that commits its draws after the swap is not covered by that fence,
so the frame can reach the panel with a region still undrawn -- cleared black --
and because the region belongs to the content, the black block moves with the
picture while scrolling. gpu_drops does not see these: the old fence did pass.

Take a fresh fence immediately before handing the frame over and wait for it,
bounded at ~16 ms so a stuck GPU cannot stop the display. This makes "the
picture is complete" a property of the moment of submission instead of the
moment the swap arrived.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -2460,6 +2460,21 @@
 	f.dst_y = (uint32_t)(fPadY < 0 ? 0 : fPadY);
 	f.dst_w = dstW;
 	f.dst_h = dstH;
+	/*
+	 * 0281: the panel reads this surface directly, so every draw into it must have finished. The
+	 * 0229 gate fences only the work submitted before the swap arrived; a compositor that commits
+	 * its draws later in the frame is not covered by that fence, and the still-undrawn region shows
+	 * up as a black block that moves with the content. Drain the GPU to "now" before handing the
+	 * frame over. Bounded at ~16 ms so a stuck GPU cannot stop the display.
+	 */
+	{
+		const uint32_t fenceNow = sweet_gpu_fence_snapshot();
+		if (fenceNow != 0) {
+			for (unsigned i = 0; i < 800 && !sweet_gpu_fence_passed(fenceNow); i++) {
+				IODelay(20);
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	/* A nonzero result is returned only before show programs or triggers the pipe. */
 	if (sweet_scanout_show(&f) != 0) {
 		sweet_hold(s, false);
